<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46565" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summissĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subm-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		summitto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a letting down</i>, <i>lowering</i>,
				<i>dropping</i>, <i>sinking</i>
			(Ciceron.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex contentione vocis et summissione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 1, 41, 146</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(iterationes) erunt ab hac summissione
					orationis alienae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Or. 25, 85</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec elatio nec summissio,</span>”
				i. e. <i>depression</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Top. 18, 71</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
